Background-worker now runs some scheduled jobs. The background-worker configuration exposes the job dispatcher, worker, retry, shutdown, and reaper settings under `scheduledJobs`; all settings default to the current behavior. `scheduledJobs.workerThreads` defaults to `1`, so no operator action is required when the default parallelism is sufficient.
Scheduled jobs currently use separate `meetings` and `conversations` queues, with one worker pool assigned to each queue.
Each background-worker instance uses one additional PostgreSQL connection for scheduled-job coordination; increasing `workerThreads` does not increase the connection count.

The Helm chart sets `background-worker.terminationGracePeriodSeconds` to `40`, providing a margin over the default `scheduledJobs.gracefulShutdownTimeout` of `30s`. Adjust both settings together if changing the shutdown timeout.
